          {
            "title": "Creating",
            "id": 88780,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>When we want to use our class template to create something, we start by creating a variable, like <code>fluffy</code> here.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"class\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"VirtualPet\" class=\"title\" /><text value=\":\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  color = \" /><text value=\"&quot;brown&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"fluffy =\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"37\" endIndex=\"43\" /><option startIndex=\"44\" endIndex=\"45\" /></options></interaction></interactions></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>fluffy</code>, followed by <code>=</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>When we want to use our class template to create something, we start by creating a variable, like <code>fluffy</code> here.</p><p>Begin the line that will hold a new pet named <code>fluffy</code>.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"class\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"VirtualPet\" class=\"title\" /><text value=\":\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  color = \" /><text value=\"&quot;brown&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"fluffy =\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"37\" endIndex=\"43\" /><option startIndex=\"44\" endIndex=\"45\" /><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"==\" /></content></option><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"VirtualPet\" /></content></option></options></interaction></interactions></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>fluffy</code>, followed by <code>=</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeSelected": true
          },
          {
            "title": "Parentheses ",
            "id": 89037,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Next, we add the class name and parentheses to create it, like with <code>VirtualPet()</code> here.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"class\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"VirtualPet\" class=\"title\" /><text value=\":\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  color = \" /><text value=\"&quot;brown&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"fluffy = VirtualPet()\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"46\" endIndex=\"56\" /><option startIndex=\"56\" endIndex=\"57\" /><option startIndex=\"57\" endIndex=\"58\" /></options></interaction></interactions></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>VirtualPet</code>, followed by <code>(</code>, and finally <code>)</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Next, we add the class name and parentheses to create the instance.</p><p>Create the pet by calling the <code>VirtualPet</code> template.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"class\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"VirtualPet\" class=\"title\" /><text value=\":\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  color = \" /><text value=\"&quot;brown&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"fluffy = VirtualPet()\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"46\" endIndex=\"56\" /><option startIndex=\"56\" endIndex=\"57\" /><option startIndex=\"57\" endIndex=\"58\" /><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"[\" /></content></option><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"]\" /></content></option></options></interaction></interactions></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>VirtualPet</code>, followed by <code>(</code>, and finally <code>)</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeSelected": true
          },
          {
            "title": "Instances",
            "id": 89348,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>When we create variables from the class template, we're creating <strong>instances</strong>. <code>fluffy</code> and <code>benny</code> are instances of the <code>VirtualPet</code> class.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"class\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"VirtualPet\" class=\"title\" /><text value=\":\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  color = \" /><text value=\"&quot;brown&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"fluffy = VirtualPet()\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"benny = VirtualPet()\" /><text type=\"break\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"59\" endIndex=\"64\" /><option startIndex=\"65\" endIndex=\"66\" /><option startIndex=\"67\" endIndex=\"79\" /></options></interaction></interactions></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>benny</code>, followed by <code>=</code>, and finally <code>VirtualPet()</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>When we create variables from the class template, we're creating <strong>instances</strong>. <code>fluffy</code> and <code>benny</code> are instances of the <code>VirtualPet</code> class.</p><p>Add a second instance named <code>benny</code>.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"class\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"VirtualPet\" class=\"title\" /><text value=\":\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  color = \" /><text value=\"&quot;brown&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"fluffy = VirtualPet()\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"benny = VirtualPet()\" /><text type=\"break\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"59\" endIndex=\"64\" /><option startIndex=\"65\" endIndex=\"66\" /><option startIndex=\"67\" endIndex=\"79\" /><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"fluffy\" /></content></option><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"VirtualPet[]\" /></content></option></options></interaction></interactions></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>benny</code>, followed by <code>=</code>, and finally <code>VirtualPet()</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeSelected": true
          },
          {
            "title": "Definition",
            "id": 88762,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>The <code>VirtualPet</code> class we're using to create the <code>fluffy</code> variables is called the <strong>definition</strong>. <code>VirtualPet</code> is the definition, <code>fluffy</code> is an instance.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"class\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"VirtualPet\" class=\"title\" /><text value=\":\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  color = \" /><text value=\"&quot;brown&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  legs = \" /><text value=\"4\" class=\"number\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  lives = \" /><text value=\"&quot;9&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"fluffy = VirtualPet()\" /></content></code></body></html>",
            "hardModeSelected": true
          },
          {
            "title": "Variable",
            "id": 88764,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>To access a class variable, we add the instance name, a <code>.</code>, and the name of the variable we want, like <code>skippy.wagging_tail</code> here.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"class\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"VirtualPet\" class=\"title\" /><text value=\":\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  wagging_tail = \" /><text value=\"True\" class=\"literal\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  color = \" /><text value=\"&quot;brown&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"skippy = VirtualPet()\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"print(skippy.wagging_tail)\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"87\" endIndex=\"93\" /><option startIndex=\"93\" endIndex=\"94\" /><option startIndex=\"94\" endIndex=\"106\" /></options></interaction></interactions><output><content><text value=\"True\" /></content></output></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>skippy</code>, followed by <code>.</code>, and finally <code>wagging_tail</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>To access a class variable, we add the instance name, a <code>.</code>, and the name of the variable we want.</p><p>Use the instance <code>skippy</code> to read its tail state and print <code>True</code>.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"class\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"VirtualPet\" class=\"title\" /><text value=\":\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  wagging_tail = \" /><text value=\"True\" class=\"literal\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  color = \" /><text value=\"&quot;brown&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"skippy = VirtualPet()\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"print(skippy.wagging_tail)\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"87\" endIndex=\"93\" /><option startIndex=\"93\" endIndex=\"94\" /><option startIndex=\"94\" endIndex=\"106\" /><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"color\" /></content></option><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"VirtualPet\" /></content></option></options></interaction></interactions><output><content><text value=\"True\" /></content></output></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>skippy</code>, followed by <code>.</code>, and finally <code>wagging_tail</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeSelected": true
          },
          {
            "title": "Other instances",
            "id": 89039,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>We can access all of the variables we created in the class definition. We access the value of the variable <code>color</code> by coding <code>skippy.color</code>.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"class\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"VirtualPet\" class=\"title\" /><text value=\":\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  wagging_tail = \" /><text value=\"True\" class=\"literal\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  color = \" /><text value=\"&quot;brown&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"skippy = VirtualPet()\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"print(skippy.wagging_tail)\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"print(skippy.color)\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"validatedInput\" isDefault=\"true\" startIndex=\"114\" endIndex=\"126\" /></interactions><output><content><text value=\"True\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"brown\" /></content></output></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to type <code>skippy.color</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Question 1",
            "id": 88779,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Which piece of code correctly creates an instance of a class called <code>Cat</code>?</p><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\"><code>fluffy = Cat()</code></item><item value=\"4\" correct=\"false\"><code>fluffy = VirtualPet()</code></item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\"><code>fluffy = Cat()</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>A program has a class named <code>Cat</code>. Which line creates a <code>Cat</code> instance named <code>fluffy</code>?</p><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\"><code>fluffy = Cat()</code></item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\"><code>fluffy = Cat</code></item><item value=\"3\" correct=\"false\"><code>Cat = fluffy()</code></item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>fluffy = Cat()</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Question 2",
            "id": 89473,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>What does this code do?</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"class\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"VirtualPet\" class=\"title\" /><text value=\":\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  color = \" /><text value=\"&quot;brown&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"fluffy = VirtualPet()\" /></content></code><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\">We're defining a class and creating an instance of it</item><item value=\"4\" correct=\"false\">We're only defining a class</item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">We're defining a class and creating an instance of it.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>After this code runs, what do <code>VirtualPet</code> and <code>fluffy</code> represent?</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"class\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"VirtualPet\" class=\"title\" /><text value=\":\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  color = \" /><text value=\"&quot;brown&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"fluffy = VirtualPet()\" /></content></code><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\"><code>VirtualPet</code> is a class and <code>fluffy</code> is its instance</item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\">Both names represent classes</item><item value=\"3\" correct=\"false\"><code>fluffy</code> is a class and <code>VirtualPet</code> is its instance</item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\"><code>VirtualPet</code> is a class and <code>fluffy</code> is its instance.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeSelected": true
          },
          {
            "title": "Question 3",
            "id": 88781,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>What's happening in this code?</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"class\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"VirtualPet\" class=\"title\" /><text value=\":\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  wagging_tail = \" /><text value=\"True\" class=\"literal\" /></content></code><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\">We're defining a class</item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\">We're creating a class instance</item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">We're defining a class.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Why does this code define a class but create no <code>VirtualPet</code> instance?</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"class\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"VirtualPet\" class=\"title\" /><text value=\":\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  wagging_tail = \" /><text value=\"True\" class=\"literal\" /></content></code><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\">It never calls <code>VirtualPet()</code></item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\">The <code>wagging_tail</code> variable automatically creates an instance</item><item value=\"3\" correct=\"false\">Writing the class body also creates one unnamed instance</item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">It never calls <code>VirtualPet()</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Question 4",
            "id": 89474,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>What's the correct way to access an instance's variable?</p><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\"><code>instance.variable</code></item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\"><code>instance(variable)</code></item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>instance.variable</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>We access an instance's variable by writing the instance name, a dot, and the variable name.</p><p>An instance named <code>fluffy</code> has a variable named <code>color</code>. Which expression reads it?</p><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\"><code>fluffy.color</code></item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\"><code>fluffy(color)</code></item><item value=\"3\" correct=\"false\"><code>color.fluffy</code></item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>fluffy.color</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Example 1",
            "id": 89475,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Inside the <code>print()</code> statement, display the variable <code>wagging_tail</code> of the <code>spot</code> instance.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"class\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"VirtualPet\" class=\"title\" /><text value=\":\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  wagging_tail = \" /><text value=\"True\" class=\"literal\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"spot = VirtualPet()\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"print(spot.wagging_tail)\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"67\" endIndex=\"71\" /><option startIndex=\"71\" endIndex=\"72\" /><option startIndex=\"72\" endIndex=\"84\" /><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"(\" /></content></option><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\")\" /></content></option></options></interaction></interactions><output><content><text value=\"True\" /></content></output></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>spot</code>, followed by <code>.</code>, and finally <code>wagging_tail</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Inside the <code>print()</code> statement, display the variable <code>wagging_tail</code> of the <code>spot</code> instance.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"class\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"VirtualPet\" class=\"title\" /><text value=\":\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  wagging_tail = \" /><text value=\"True\" class=\"literal\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"spot = VirtualPet()\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"print(spot.wagging_tail)\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"67\" endIndex=\"71\" /><option startIndex=\"71\" endIndex=\"72\" /><option startIndex=\"72\" endIndex=\"84\" /><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"[\" /></content></option><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"]\" /></content></option></options></interaction></interactions><output><content><text value=\"True\" /></content></output></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>spot</code>, followed by <code>.</code>, and finally <code>wagging_tail</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Example 2",
            "id": 89476,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Create an instance of the <code>Pokemon</code> class and store it in a variable called <code>pokemon</code>.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"class\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"Pokemon\" class=\"title\" /><text value=\":\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  name = \" /><text value=\"&quot;squirtle&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"pokemon = Pokemon()\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"print(pokemon.name)\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"36\" endIndex=\"43\" /><option startIndex=\"44\" endIndex=\"45\" /><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"[]\" /></content></option><option startIndex=\"46\" endIndex=\"53\" /><option startIndex=\"53\" endIndex=\"54\" /><option startIndex=\"54\" endIndex=\"55\" /></options></interaction></interactions><output><content><text value=\"squirtle\" /></content></output></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>pokemon</code> followed by <code>=</code> and then <code>Pokemon</code>, <code>(</code>, <code>)</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Create <code>pokemon</code> from <code>Pokemon</code>, then use that instance to print its <code>name</code>.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"class\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"Pokemon\" class=\"title\" /><text value=\":\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  name = \" /><text value=\"&quot;squirtle&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"pokemon = Pokemon()\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"print(pokemon.name)\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"36\" endIndex=\"43\" /><option startIndex=\"44\" endIndex=\"45\" /><option startIndex=\"46\" endIndex=\"53\" /><option startIndex=\"62\" endIndex=\"69\" /><option startIndex=\"70\" endIndex=\"74\" /><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"==\" /></content></option><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"&quot;pokemon&quot;\" /></content></option><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"color\" /></content></option></options></interaction></interactions><output><content><text value=\"squirtle\" /></content></output></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>pokemon</code>, followed by <code>=</code>, <code>Pokemon</code>, <code>pokemon</code>, and finally <code>name</code>.</p></body></html>",
